fact WorkItem(id: "WI-871", description: some(value: "A COMPONENTWISE PROVIDER'S SECOND REQUIREMENT SLOT IS READ FROM THE FIRST WHEN THE FIRST'S CARRIER IS THE PROVIDER ITSELF — a WI-857 dictionary-slot defect, PRE-EXISTING, surfaced by WI-858 and now reachable from the SHIPPED prelude. REPRODUCER (measured at WI-858's HEAD, and on a purely LOCAL carrier with no prelude and no 058 vocabulary — a two-parameter enum with `requires PartialEq[A], requires PartialEq[B]`, `provides PartialEq[Self]`, and a componentwise `eq` body calling `PartialEq.eq(al, bl)` then `PartialEq.eq(ar, br)`): comparing two values whose FIRST component is itself that carrier and whose SECOND is a primitive dies at eval with `match_failed(occurrence: Node, scrutinee: 7)` — the second component's compare dispatched to the CARRIER's own `eq`, which then matched a primitive against the carrier's entity pattern. CHARACTERIZED BY DRIVING, four cells: A=<carrier>,B=<primitive> FAILS; A=<primitive>,B=<carrier> PASSES; A=B=<carrier> PASSES; A,B both primitive PASSES. So it is not 'nesting' as such — it is the slot the FIRST component's requirement occupies once that requirement resolves to the provider ITSELF. SUSPECT (not confirmed — confirm by driving before fixing): the WI-857 LOCALITY rule (resolve_inner's `local_provider` filter, 058 §3.8) narrows candidates to the enclosing provider whenever that provider offers the spec, and both slots carry the SAME spec at DIFFERENT bindings; the filter is documented as binding-matched (candidates are head-matched first), so the divergence may instead be in how the body's two same-spec reads are INDEXED into the provider half of dict_layout. Whichever it is, it is one owner and the four-cell matrix above is the oracle. IMPACT: `PartialEq.eq(pair(fst: pair(fst: 1, snd: 2), snd: 7), …)` on the shipped `anthill.prelude.Pair` fails at eval; before WI-858 gave Pair a componentwise `eq` the same expression answered correctly via the structural builtin, so this is a user-visible regression for that shape and the reason it is filed rather than absorbed. PINNED at wi858_pair_orderings_test::a_nested_pair_in_the_first_component_is_a_recorded_defect, whose passing arms are the control and whose failing arm PANICS WITH INSTRUCTIONS when the defect is fixed. ACCEPTANCE: all four cells of the matrix pass on both the local carrier and the prelude Pair; the recorded-defect arm is folded into pair_equality_is_componentwise; wi857_dictionary_layout_test unchanged; full workspace green via rustland/scripts/test.sh. REFERENCE: design/058-implementation.md §7 (the layout and its one owner, dict_layout); wi857_dictionary_layout_test; stdlib/anthill/prelude/pair.anthill's header."), context: none, acceptance: [ToolPasses(tool: "cargo-test", params: none)], depends_on: some(value: nil), generates: none, requires_capability: none, status: Delivered(agent: "claude", at: "2026-08-08T18:04:34Z"))

